UTIF 3.1.0 / viewer-1: JPEG implementations replaced
===================================================

UTIF upstream commit: 27f1098a67c3cfd4348c9b8fd887fcd8cd171095
https://github.com/photopea/UTIF.js/tree/27f1098a67c3cfd4348c9b8fd887fcd8cd171095
The supplied TIFF source is an adaptation of this revision, not a byte-for-byte
copy. Photopea's own TIFF code retains the MIT notice in UTIF-LICENSE.

Modifications by Ilya Barilo:
- The entire minified ordinary JPEG decoder IIFE was removed.
- The entire UTIF.LosslessJpegDecode implementation was removed.
- The previous old/new JPEG-in-TIFF adapter functions were removed.
- JPEG dispatch no longer mistakes a compressed strip for uncompressed bytes
  when its input length happens to equal the output buffer length.
- CMYK without alpha produces an opaque final pixel.
- Private MakerNote/DNG directories are not automatically decoded for image display.

The source is supplied as sources/utif/UTIF.js. The transformation script
scripts/prepare-utif.cjs verifies the original revision's SHA-256 before removing
the old implementations. The original file containing those implementations is
not included in this distribution.

JPEG decoding now uses libjpeg-turbo 3.2.0 through our separate MIT C/JS bridge.
The TIFF Worker installs our adapters from src/core/tiff-jpeg.mjs.
The JPEG library and runtime retain their original conditions and attribution:
see JPEG-NOTICE, libjpeg-turbo-README.ijg, libjpeg-turbo-LICENSE and
JPEG-RUNTIME-NOTICE. Our separate adapters are Copyright (c) 2026 Ilya Barilo, MIT.

